WEBVTT

00:11:59.792 --> 00:12:01.476
We're fighting for justice

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:04.434
for Ahmaud Arbery, Breonna Taylor
and George Floyd,

00:12:04.458 --> 00:12:06.143
we're also fighting for justice

00:12:06.167 --> 00:12:08.726
for other folks whose names
you haven't heard,

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:10.143
Nina Pop and others,

00:12:10.167 --> 00:12:13.351
whose stories of injustice

00:12:13.375 --> 00:12:16.309
and the relationship
to the criminal justice system

00:12:16.333 --> 00:12:21.434
represent all the ways
in which fighting right now is important.

00:12:21.458 --> 00:12:22.893
Over the last couple of years,

00:12:22.917 --> 00:12:24.684
we have worked to build a movement,

00:12:24.708 --> 00:12:27.059
to hold district attorneys accountable

00:12:27.083 --> 00:12:30.643
and to change the role
of district attorneys in our country.